From f0078aee30cbecc1ec3ec0709345931d0edae45e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:20:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: remove bitcoin-qt

Lotus V2 drops the Qt wallet GUI; wallets are operated through RPC and
lotus-cli. Remove the GUI and everything that existed only to build,
package, test or document it.

Deleted:
- src/qt/, share/qt/, cmake/modules/FindQREncode.cmake and the
  translation script, contrib/bitcoin-qt.pro, the Qt .prl converter,
  the macOS app deployment and detached-signature scripts, the Debian
  bitcoin-qt package files and AUR bitcoin-abc-qt package, the
  Transifex config, translation tooling and translation docs, and the
  Qt5 arcanist linter.
- The 15 Qt-only depends recipes (qt, qrencode, expat, fontconfig,
  freetype, X11/xcb/xkb libraries) and their patches.

Edited:
- CMake: remove BUILD_QT, ENABLE_BIP70, ENABLE_QRCODE and
  ENABLE_DBUS_NOTIFICATIONS, their native-build flags, the qt
  subdirectory and the USE_QRCODE/USE_DBUS/ENABLE_BIP70 config
  defines. Passing one of them now only gives CMake's unused-variable
  warning, so existing build scripts keep working.
- depends: remove NO_QT, NO_QR and the Qt package lists.
- Guix: build the macOS tarball with plain `cmake --install` as on
  Linux, drop the app signing step and the GUI-only symbol-check
  allowances (xkb version, X11/font libraries, GUI frameworks/DLLs).
- NSIS installer: no GUI executable, shortcuts or URL handler.
- Packaging, CI and lint: Debian control/rules/copyright, TeamCity
  (Qt test suite, build-without-qt and build-without-bip70), the
  Windows test script, the Bookworm dependency list, the functional
  test PATH, expected circular dependencies, and sanitizer
  suppressions.
- Comments and documentation no longer describe bitcoin-qt.

Kept: protobuf and cpython recipes (Chronik), share/pixmaps (installer
images), the node/wallet/chain interfaces and ui_interface, the "qt"
log category (rpc_misc.py toggles it) and the hidden GUI arguments that
let a config file shared with older GUI releases still parse.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Native Qt/ZeroMQ dependency removal preserves new HTTP2/nghttp2 feature flags, helper configuration and OpenSSL3.5 chain; no removed Qt/ZMQ code is restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
